 "sections": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "Seeing Children Today",
   "html": "<p>Inspiring the Confident, Compassionate and Creative leaders of tomorrow</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://sunflowercreativearts.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/2018-2019-annual-report-cover-3.png",
    "alt": ""
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "Sunflower Creative Arts | Annual Report 2018-2019",
   "html": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "WE SEE CHILDREN",
   "html": "<p>Throughout 2018/2019, across all our Sunflower programs, teachers, parents and student observers have SEEN first-hand that experiences in play, nature and the arts are essential for healthy human development.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/33944192188_649f2d5eb1_c.jpg",
    "alt": "Untitled"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "4460 parent volunteer/co-op hours allowed teachers to provide optimal play-based experiences for children in Sunflower programs.",
   "html": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49011611886_ac9759b2e2_c.jpg",
    "alt": "Untitled"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p><strong>Who have newly mastered a skill</strong><strong>,</strong>empathize with and eagerly assist other children who are still learning.</p>\n<p><em>This year <strong>254</strong>families benefited from a play-based education in <strong>18</strong>weekly programs at our Sunflower campus</em></p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "gallery",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49011813557_4c881f7ab9_c.jpg",
     "alt": "DSC_0014"
    },
    {
     "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49016503933_22a9f432fa_c.jpg",
     "alt": "Untitled"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p>“When we talk about really seeing children, we mean truly being with them. In Silence. With no agenda. It is only then that we can see the capability, intelligence, caring, curiosity and depth of passion in every molecule of their being.”</p>\n<p>Susan Caruso, Executive Director and Founder, Sunflower Creative Arts</p>\n<p>Who care for the world, who have the initiative to use their voices and creatively use materials to display their caring.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "gallery",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49112686233_f4eb078a1e_c.jpg",
     "alt": "Untitled"
    },
    {
     "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49119346236_b89c0dc4b1_o.jpg",
     "alt": "1V3A00765d mark 4"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p><strong>Ruth Floreal,</strong>Doctor of Education, conducted a study at Sunflower Creative Arts on incorporating STEM into early childhood:</p>\n<p><em>Children at Sunflower have uninterrupted play time because their play is their work. Play is when children get the opportunity to think, reason and build the confidence to be independent…children build the confidence to be reflective decision makers and are empowered to speak up for themselves.</em></p>\n<p><em>Excerpt from the doctoral thesis of Ruth Floreal, Ed.D.,</em><em>Northeastern University School of Professional Studies</em></p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "WE OPENED OUR DOORS",
   "html": "<p>This year we opened our doors to graduate as well as undergraduate students and in-service teachers to SEE children and the transformative power of learning in a play-based environment, where adults facilitate exploration guided by each child’s unique wonder, curiosity and interests.</p>\n<p><strong>Who feel safe to utilize materials in unique ways,</strong>allowing their curiosity to guide their learning.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49119418551_c6b9c53b2f_c.jpg",
    "alt": "Untitled"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p>At Sunflower, children are given the space to explore natural phenomena, test (and retest) hypotheses and adjust based on what they learn, which by definition shares a lot of the key components of the scientific method of discovery. <em>Scott Cooper, Sunflower Parent</em></p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "SUNFLOWER OUTREACH",
   "html": "<p>Through the bold outreach efforts of our Sunflower Play Initiative, we are encouraging the Delray and greater community to SEE play as a critical cross-cultural component of childhood, crucial for every aspect of learning and growth.</p>\n<h3><strong>Sunflower Play Initiative</strong></h3>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7842/33124570788_3ffa59da22_c.jpg",
    "alt": "DSC_0528"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p><strong>Mission:</strong>To shine a light on the profound power of play</p>\n<p><strong>Vision:</strong>To bring back child-directed free play to every child’s life, everyday</p>\n<p><strong>Year 1:</strong>We hosted over 20 Pop-Up playful builds with over 1,000 total attendees.</p>\n<p><strong>The Play Initiative partnered with:</strong>Delray Beach Children’s Garden/ Milagro Afterschool Program/Farmworker Coordinating Council of Palm Beach County, Inc./Delray Beach Public Library/Delray Parks and Recreation/Arts Garage/Wise Tribe</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49119676827_8f0f413790_o.jpg",
    "alt": "GfNVO9pxSv2S73ZG2rm8sQ_thumb_29fa"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p>“I work here. It is always quiet. I never hear the sounds of children. I have no children of my own. No nieces or nephews. Nothing. The children are always quiet, serious, shy, afraid. Now you are here. . . . I’m working and it’s not quiet. I hear laughter and joy, children talking, planning, playing. They are happy. They are having fun. It is good to see them being kids, being real kids, having a childhood.</p>\n<p><em>Sergio M. Palacio, Executive Director, Farmworker’s Coordinating Council of Palm Beach County, Inc.</em></p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "2018-2019 COMPLIMENTARY COMMUNITY EVENTS",
   "html": "<h3><strong>Community Presentation of the Sunflower Play Initiative</strong></h3>\n<p>Founder and Director, <strong>Susan Caruso</strong>, along with Simone Chin, Assistant Director of the Sunflower Play Initiative, presented to the Delray Beach Chamber of Commerce Nonprofit Council about the Play Initiative. This year Susan made presentations about the significance of play as far away as South Carolina and Maryland, extending Sunflower’s reach.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49118997073_a75a364bb1_c.jpg",
    "alt": "IMG_3174 copy"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p><strong>Who thrive when we all come together as a community</strong>to support them in ways that spark their creativity, grow their confidence and encourage curiosity.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/4828/46273404384_23e84245cb_c.jpg",
    "alt": "0K7A7992"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p>Over 500 people attended our <strong>Ice Castle Festival & Play Day</strong>, our annual community celebration of Play + Nature + Art. 500 Volunteer hours made this event happen!</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/1962/44111949134_bd3e22f3f0_c.jpg",
    "alt": "Untitled"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p>Our <strong>Sunflower Roots & Shoots Club,</strong>a part of Jane Goodall’s worldwide kids’ activist group, allows us to SEE children performing service projects together that demonstrate concern for the environment, animals and the human community.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": "WE SEE YOUR GENEROSITY",
   "html": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7869/46638178874_ac051688a7_c.jpg",
    "alt": "HSJ 2019-37"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p><strong>7942</strong>Total Volunteer Hours.</p>\n<p><strong>$24,156 raised</strong>for programs at our annual Hop, Skip & a Jump-A-Thon</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://live.staticflickr.com/4854/46239605734_5bd2bc905d_c.jpg",
    "alt": "Untitled"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p>During Great Give 2019, <strong>$18,594 raised</strong>from generous donations and matching funds to support Sunflower’s need-based Scholarship Fund.</p>\n<p><strong>14 Business Sponsors</strong>supported our Community Events.</p>\n<p><strong>Over $21,000</strong>in Capital Fund donations. Remaining Goal: <strong>$586,000</strong></p>\n<p>Thanks Batchelor Foundation for your continued support! A <strong>$20,000 Batchelor grant</strong>supported our need-based Scholarship Fund.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "image": {
    "src": "https://sunflowercreativearts.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/2018-2019-Financials.png",
    "alt": ""
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "heading": null,
   "html": "<p><strong>Thank you for your generous donations.</strong></p>\n<p>Every effort has been made to acknowledge contributions correctly and completely from July 1, 2018 to June 30, 2019. Should you discover an error or omission, please call us at 561 501-6615.</p>\n<h3>A Home for Sunflower Capital Campaign Donors</h3>\n<p>* Indicates 2018-19 Donor</p>"
  },
